.policy "python-security-code-injection" revision 1
.description "Never let client request data reach Python evaluation, imports, pickle-style or unsafe YAML deserializers, or a template's source; parse it as data instead."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*.py"
// Rerail's own rule, not a port. It reports a call that turns client request data into code the server runs, when
// the value comes from a request in the same function or through the project's helpers across files (lib/security's
// sec_tainted: Django/DRF request attributes, uploaded file content, Flask's request, Starlette's request, FastAPI
// and Flask route parameters). Three sink families, a message each:
//   interpreters    builtins eval/exec/compile, importlib.import_module, __import__: their first argument;
//   deserializers   pickle/_pickle/cPickle loads/load/Unpickler, cloudpickle and dill loads/load, joblib.load,
//                   pandas.read_pickle, marshal loads/load, shelve.open's path, jsonpickle decode/loads,
//                   yaml.unsafe_load(_all), yaml.full_load(_all), and yaml.load(_all) whose Loader is missing or is
//                   not a safe one (SafeLoader, CSafeLoader, BaseLoader, CBaseLoader, a class of the run deriving
//                   from one, or an expression whose text names one): their first argument;
//   template source flask/quart render_template_string, jinja2.Template, django.template.Template,
//                   mako.template.Template (first positional, or source=/template_string=/text=), and
//                   `<env>.from_string(src)` on a jinja2 Environment (NativeEnvironment, a subclass of the run), a
//                   Django Engine (`Engine(...)`, `Engine.get_default()`, `engines["django"]`), a name bound to one,
//                   or a receiver named like a template environment (`app.jinja_env`, `self.env`, `templates.engine`).
//   def restore(request):
//       pickle.loads(request.body)                                   reported
//       render_template_string("<p>" + request.args["n"] + "</p>")   reported: the value is template source
//       render_template_string("<p>{{ n }}</p>", n=request.args["n"]) not reported: render context is data
//       yaml.load(request.body, Loader=yaml.SafeLoader)              not reported
// Left alone: json.loads, yaml.safe_load, ast.literal_eval, django.core.signing.loads and itsdangerous loads (library
// calls stop the taint), eval of a constant, pickle of what the server wrote (cache, Redis, Celery results: no request
// source), `SandboxedEnvironment`/`ImmutableSandboxedEnvironment` receivers (and an unresolved environment in a file
// that builds a sandbox), `torch.load` without `weights_only=False` (the default is True from torch 2.6; the python
// pack's bandit-b614 flags every call), test files. Sanitisers it trusts: lib/security's sec_checked_expr (the value
// passes a check call or an `in` allow-list test in its function, so `if fmt in ALLOWED: import_module(...)` is
// silent; a function that itself evaluates, such as `validate_expr(e)` running `eval`, is no check), and, for
// deserializers, a payload the same function also passes to an `hmac` call (verified before use). The taint goes
// through byte decoders (`bytes.fromhex`, binascii, codecs, zlib/gzip/bz2/lzma, `io.BytesIO`), so a compressed or
// hex-encoded pickle in a cookie is reported.
// A Django `Template` or Django `Engine.from_string` gets its own message: the Django template language cannot call
// arbitrary code, but a client template reads whatever its context reaches (settings, related objects).
// Gaps: a jinja2 sandbox stays a mitigation (sandbox escapes exist), so a sandboxed environment is not reported even
// though user templates there are still risky; values stored on objects or in the database and read back later (the
// changedetection.io advisory's stored template) are not followed; an hmac check after the load is still trusted;
// ruamel.yaml's unsafe typ and Flask-Session's pickle backends are not matched; a DRF serializer's `validate(data)` or
// a form's own `self.cleaned_data` in `clean()` are not sources (netbox's uploaded-script `exec` is reached that way).
#include "lib/security.rerail"

// Per file and across files (lib/security's origins): each sink states what reaches it by origin (sec_fhit), and a
// finding reads the cross-file answer by the sink's term (sec_xfirst). A `from_string` receiver bound to a module
// variable of another file (`from app.templating import env`) is a template environment by that module's say
// (ci_xvar, by the variable's qualified name), so a `from_string` call is a sink by the cross-file answer (ci_xfs).
// A finding names the first source its sink takes (sec_xfirst by the sink's term), so one sink is reported once.
.violation Interpreter(at: node, callee: symbol, what: symbol, p: symbol, l: number) "{callee} runs {what} ({p}:{l}) as Python code. Parse it as data (json, ast.literal_eval) or map it through an allow-list; leave it only for a deliberate, admin-only scripting feature."
Interpreter(c, cn, what, p, l) :- ci_sink(c, "interp", _), pt_tm(c, ct), sec_xfirst("interp", ct, k),
    sec_src_info(k, what, p, l), ci_callee_text(c, cn).

.violation Deserializer(at: node, callee: symbol, what: symbol, p: symbol, l: number) "{callee} deserializes {what} ({p}:{l}), and a crafted payload runs code. Accept JSON (json.loads, yaml.safe_load) or verify an HMAC first; leave it if the bytes are server-written."
Deserializer(c, cn, what, p, l) :- ci_sink(c, "deser", _), pt_tm(c, ct), sec_xfirst("deser", ct, k),
    sec_src_info(k, what, p, l), ci_callee_text(c, cn).

.violation TemplateSource(at: node, callee: symbol, what: symbol, p: symbol, l: number) "{what} ({p}:{l}) is template source for {callee}, so a client can run code. Use a fixed template and pass the value as render context; a jinja2 sandbox only mitigates."
TemplateSource(c, cn, what, p, l) :- ci_sink(c, "template", _), !ci_django_template(c), pt_tm(c, ct),
    sec_xfirst("template", ct, k), sec_src_info(k, what, p, l), ci_callee_text(c, cn).
TemplateSource(c, cn, what, p, l) :- ci_fs_sink(c, _), pt_tm(c, ct), ci_xfs(ct, "tpl"), sec_xfirst("fs", ct, k),
    sec_src_info(k, what, p, l), ci_callee_text(c, cn).
.violation DjangoTemplateSource(at: node, callee: symbol, what: symbol, p: symbol, l: number) "{what} ({p}:{l}) is Django template source for {callee}, so a client can read any value its context reaches. Use a fixed template and pass the value as render context."
DjangoTemplateSource(c, cn, what, p, l) :- ci_sink(c, "template", _), ci_django_template(c), pt_tm(c, ct),
    sec_xfirst("template", ct, k), sec_src_info(k, what, p, l), ci_callee_text(c, cn).
DjangoTemplateSource(c, cn, what, p, l) :- ci_fs_sink(c, _), pt_tm(c, ct), ci_xfs(ct, "dj"), sec_xfirst("fs", ct, k),
    sec_src_info(k, what, p, l), ci_callee_text(c, cn).
// The functions that run code are this rule's sinks: a validator-named one is no check.
sec_sink_fn(gq) :- ci_sink(c, _, _), nearest(c, g, fdef), pt_def(g, gq).
sec_sink_fn(gq) :- ci_fs_sink(c, _), pt_tm(c, ct), ci_xfs(ct, _), nearest(c, g, fdef), pt_def(g, gq).

// What each sink takes (sec_tainted): sink call c, outside test code, takes argument a, which holds client data,
// unless a is a value its function checked (ci_checked); a check call of the run passes it through a gate that holds
// where that check reaches this rule's sink (`G|e:cic:…|`). A deserializer's payload its function also verifies with
// hmac is none.
sec_fhit(fam, c, o) :- ci_sink(c, fam, a), ci_live(c, a), sec_tainted(a, o), !sec_echk_any("cic", a),
    !ci_hmac_fam(fam, a).
sec_fhit(fam, c, g) :- ci_sink(c, fam, a), ci_live(c, a), sec_tainted(a, _), sec_egate("cic", "t", a, g),
    !ci_hmac_fam(fam, a).
sec_fhit("fs", c, o) :- ci_fs_sink(c, a), ci_live(c, a), sec_tainted(a, o), !sec_echk_any("cic", a).
sec_fhit("fs", c, g) :- ci_fs_sink(c, a), ci_live(c, a), sec_tainted(a, _), sec_egate("cic", "t", a, g).
sec_gin(g, o) :- (ci_sink(_, _, a) ; ci_fs_sink(_, a)), sec_tainted(a, o), sec_egate("cic", "t", a, g).
// ci_live(c, a): code argument a of call c, outside test code, is not checked.
.decl ci_live(c: node, a: node)
ci_live(c, a) :- (ci_sink(c, _, a) ; ci_fs_sink(c, a)), docof(c, d), !sec_test_doc(d), !ci_checked(a).
.decl ci_hmac_fam(fam: symbol, a: node)
ci_hmac_fam("deser", a) :- ci_hmac_checked(a).
// ci_checked(a): sink argument a holds a checked value (sec_checked_expr), or reads, anywhere inside it (an f-string,
// a concatenation), a name its function checks (`if fmt not in ALLOWED: …` then `import_module(f"pkg.{fmt}")`). The
// same by a check call of the run (sec_echk_c "cic", decided across files).
.decl ci_checked(a: node)
ci_checked(a) :- sec_checked_expr(a).
ci_checked(a) :- ci_reads_in(a, h, x), sec_checked(h, x).
sec_echk_c("cic", a, t) :- (ci_sink(_, _, a) ; ci_fs_sink(_, a)), sec_checked_expr_c(a, t).
sec_echk_c("cic", a, t) :- (ci_sink(_, _, a) ; ci_fs_sink(_, a)), ci_reads_in(a, h, x), sec_checked_c(h, x, t).
// ci_reads_in(a, h, x): expression a, in scope h, reads name x anywhere inside it.
.decl ci_reads_in(a: node, h: node, x: symbol)
ci_reads_in(a, h, x) :- (ci_sink(_, _, a) ; ci_fs_sink(_, a)), has(a, i, "identifier"), text(i, x),
    !field(_, "attribute", i), nearest(a, h, fscope).
.decl ci_callee_text(c: node, t: symbol)
ci_callee_text(c, t) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), text(f, t).

// ---- sinks -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ci_sink(c, family, a): call c runs argument a as code: family "interp", "deser" or "template". A `from_string`
// call is ci_fs_sink's.
.decl ci_sink(c: node, family: symbol, a: node)
ci_sink(c, fam, a) :- sec_call_q(c, q), ci_first_arg_q(q, fam), ci_first_arg(c, q, a), !ci_yaml_safe_call(c).
// `torch.load(f, weights_only=False)` and `numpy.load(f, allow_pickle=True)` unpickle what they read.
ci_sink(c, "deser", a) :- sec_call_q(c, "torch.load"), sec_arg(c, -1, "weights_only", v), kind(v, "false"),
    (sec_arg(c, 0, "", a) ; sec_arg(c, -1, "f", a)).
ci_sink(c, "deser", a) :- (sec_call_q(c, "numpy.load") ; sec_call_q(c, "numpy.lib.npyio.load")),
    sec_arg(c, -1, "allow_pickle", v), kind(v, "true"), (sec_arg(c, 0, "", a) ; sec_arg(c, -1, "file", a)).
// ci_django_template(c): template sink c builds a Django template: `django.template.Template(…)` (a `from_string` on
// a Django Engine: ci_xfs "dj").
.decl ci_django_template(c: node)
ci_django_template(c) :- sec_call_q(c, q), (q = "django.template.Template" ; q = "django.template.base.Template").

// ci_first_arg(c, q, a): a is the code argument of call c to q: the first positional one, or the keyword that names it.
.decl ci_first_arg(c: node, q: symbol, a: node)
ci_first_arg(c, q, a) :- sec_call_q(c, q), sec_arg(c, 0, "", a).
ci_first_arg(c, q, a) :- sec_call_q(c, q), ci_code_kw(q, k), sec_arg(c, -1, k, a).
.decl ci_code_kw(q: symbol, k: symbol)
ci_code_kw(q, "source") :- ci_first_arg_q(q, _).
ci_code_kw(q, "name") :- ci_first_arg_q(q, "interp").
ci_code_kw(q, "data") :- ci_first_arg_q(q, "deser").
ci_code_kw(q, "stream") :- ci_first_arg_q(q, "deser").
ci_code_kw(q, "file") :- ci_first_arg_q(q, "deser").
ci_code_kw(q, "filename") :- ci_first_arg_q(q, "deser").
ci_code_kw(q, "filepath_or_buffer") :- ci_first_arg_q(q, "deser").
ci_code_kw(q, "string") :- ci_first_arg_q(q, "deser").
ci_code_kw(q, "template_string") :- ci_first_arg_q(q, "template").
ci_code_kw(q, "text") :- ci_first_arg_q(q, "template").

// ci_first_arg_q(q, family): the callables whose first argument is code.
.decl ci_first_arg_q(q: symbol, family: symbol)
ci_first_arg_q("builtins.eval", "interp"). ci_first_arg_q("builtins.exec", "interp").
ci_first_arg_q("builtins.compile", "interp"). ci_first_arg_q("builtins.__import__", "interp").
ci_first_arg_q("importlib.import_module", "interp"). ci_first_arg_q("importlib.__import__", "interp").
ci_first_arg_q(cat(m, f), "deser") :- ci_pickle_module(m), (f = ".loads" ; f = ".load" ; f = ".Unpickler").
ci_first_arg_q("joblib.load", "deser"). ci_first_arg_q("pandas.read_pickle", "deser").
ci_first_arg_q("marshal.loads", "deser"). ci_first_arg_q("marshal.load", "deser").
ci_first_arg_q("shelve.open", "deser"). ci_first_arg_q("shelve.DbfilenameShelf", "deser").
ci_first_arg_q("jsonpickle.decode", "deser"). ci_first_arg_q("jsonpickle.loads", "deser").
ci_first_arg_q("jsonpickle.unpickler.decode", "deser").
ci_first_arg_q("yaml.load", "deser"). ci_first_arg_q("yaml.load_all", "deser").
ci_first_arg_q("yaml.unsafe_load", "deser"). ci_first_arg_q("yaml.unsafe_load_all", "deser").
ci_first_arg_q("yaml.full_load", "deser"). ci_first_arg_q("yaml.full_load_all", "deser").
ci_first_arg_q("flask.render_template_string", "template").
ci_first_arg_q("flask.templating.render_template_string", "template").
ci_first_arg_q("quart.render_template_string", "template").
ci_first_arg_q("jinja2.Template", "template"). ci_first_arg_q("jinja2.environment.Template", "template").
ci_first_arg_q("django.template.Template", "template"). ci_first_arg_q("django.template.base.Template", "template").
ci_first_arg_q("mako.template.Template", "template").
.decl ci_pickle_module(m: symbol)
ci_pickle_module("pickle"). ci_pickle_module("_pickle"). ci_pickle_module("cPickle"). ci_pickle_module("cloudpickle").
ci_pickle_module("dill"). ci_pickle_module("pickle5").

// ---- yaml.load's Loader ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ci_yaml_safe_call(c): c is `yaml.load(…)`/`yaml.load_all(…)` with a safe Loader, keyword or second positional.
.decl ci_yaml_safe_call(c: node)
ci_yaml_safe_call(c) :- (sec_call_q(c, "yaml.load") ; sec_call_q(c, "yaml.load_all")), ci_yaml_loader(c, v),
    ci_safe_loader(v).
.decl ci_yaml_loader(c: node, v: node)
ci_yaml_loader(c, v) :- sec_arg(c, -1, "Loader", v).
ci_yaml_loader(c, v) :- sec_arg(c, 1, "", v).
// ci_safe_loader(v): loader expression v builds only plain data: a safe PyYAML loader, a class of the run deriving
// from one (the phase py_names), or an expression naming one (`getattr(yaml, "CSafeLoader", yaml.SafeLoader)`).
.decl ci_safe_loader(v: node)
ci_safe_loader(v) :- sym_of(v, q), ci_safe_loader_q(q).
ci_safe_loader(v) :- sym_of(v, q), docof(v, d), doc(d, p, _), py_names__reads_at(p, m), py_names__ancestor(m, q, b),
    ci_safe_loader_q(b).
ci_safe_loader(v) :- text(v, t), (contains("SafeLoader", t) ; contains("BaseLoader", t)).
.decl ci_safe_loader_q(q: symbol)
ci_safe_loader_q(cat(m, l)) :- (m = "yaml." ; m = "yaml.loader." ; m = "yaml.cyaml."),
    (l = "SafeLoader" ; l = "CSafeLoader" ; l = "BaseLoader" ; l = "CBaseLoader").

// ---- template environments ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ci_fs(c, r): c is `<r>.from_string(…)`. ci_fs_sink(c, a): a is its source. It is a sink on a template environment
// that is not sandboxed: one built here, or a name bound to one, or to a module variable of the run bound to one
// (ci_xfs, across files); or a receiver named like one in a file that builds no sandbox.
.decl ci_fs(c: node, r: node)
ci_fs(c, r) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, r0, "from_string"), unparen(r0, r).
.decl ci_fs_sink(c: node, a: node)
ci_fs_sink(c, a) :- ci_fs(c, _), (sec_arg(c, 0, "", a) ; sec_arg(c, -1, "source", a)).
// ci_env_kind(r, ek, o): expression r, a `from_string` receiver or what one is bound to, is a template environment of
// kind ek, by o: "env" a jinja2 Environment or Django Engine, "dj" a Django Engine, "sb" a jinja2 sandbox (o "T"); or
// it names module variable q of the run, which is one where q's module says so (o `M|<q>`, ci_xvar).
.decl ci_env_kind(r: node, ek: symbol, o: symbol)
ci_env_kind(r, "env", "T") :- ci_env_cand(r), kind(r, "call"), field(r, "function", f), ci_env_callee(f).
ci_env_kind(r, "env", "T") :- ci_env_cand(r), kind(r, "call"), field(r, "function", f), attr_of(f, o, "get_default"),
    ci_env_callee(o).
ci_env_kind(r, ek, "T") :- ci_env_cand(r), kind(r, "subscript"), field(r, "value", o), sym_of(o, q),
    (q = "django.template.engines" ; q = "django.template.utils.engines"), (ek = "env" ; ek = "dj").
ci_env_kind(r, "dj", "T") :- ci_env_cand(r), kind(r, "call"), field(r, "function", f), sym_of(f, q),
    (q = "django.template.Engine" ; q = "django.template.engine.Engine").
ci_env_kind(r, "dj", "T") :- ci_env_cand(r), kind(r, "call"), field(r, "function", f), attr_of(f, o, "get_default"),
    sym_of(o, q), (q = "django.template.Engine" ; q = "django.template.engine.Engine").
ci_env_kind(r, "sb", "T") :- ci_env_cand(r), ci_sandbox_call(r).
ci_env_kind(r, "sb", "T") :- ci_env_cand(r), text(r, t), icontains("sandbox", t).
ci_env_kind(r, ek, o) :- ci_env_cand(r), kind(r, "identifier"), text(r, x), look(r, x, h), asg(h, x, v0, _),
    unparen(v0, v), ci_env_kind(v, ek, o).
ci_env_kind(r, ek, cat("M|", q)) :- ci_env_cand(r), kind(r, "identifier"), sym_of(r, q), contains(".", q),
    (ek = "env" ; ek = "dj" ; ek = "sb").
// ci_env_cand(r): the expressions ci_env_kind reads: `from_string` receivers, what a name among them is bound to,
// and the values of this module's variables.
.decl ci_env_cand(r: node)
ci_env_cand(r) :- ci_fs(_, r).
ci_env_cand(v) :- ci_env_cand(r), kind(r, "identifier"), text(r, x), look(r, x, h), asg(h, x, v0, _), unparen(v0, v).
ci_env_cand(v) :- modnode(_, m), asg(m, _, v0, _), unparen(v0, v).
// ci_modvar(q, ek, o): module variable q of this file (`<module>.<x>`) is bound to an environment of kind ek, by o.
.decl ci_modvar(q: symbol, ek: symbol, o: symbol)
ci_modvar(cat(mq, cat(".", x)), ek, o) :- modnode(_, m), modname(m, mq), asg(m, x, v0, _), unparen(v0, v),
    ci_env_kind(v, ek, o).
// ci_xvar(q, ek): module variable q is an environment of kind ek: by its module's own binding, or through the module
// variables it names, across files by qualified name (`from app.templating import env`, decision 0691: a module's
// variable read in another file is a meant crossing, keyed by symbol), so it is declared cross_file.
.decl ci_xvar(q: symbol, ek: symbol) cross_file
ci_xvar(q, ek) :- ci_modvar(q, ek, "T").
ci_xvar(q, ek) :- ci_modvar(q, ek, o), match("M\\|(?<q2>.*)", o), ci_xvar(q2, ek).
// ci_xek(r, ek): `from_string` receiver r, by its term, is an environment of kind ek.
.decl ci_xek(r: symbol, ek: symbol) cross_file
ci_xek(rt, ek) :- ci_fs(_, r), ci_env_kind(r, ek, "T"), pt_tm(r, rt).
ci_xek(rt, ek) :- ci_fs(_, r), ci_env_kind(r, ek, o), match("M\\|(?<q>.*)", o), ci_xvar(q, ek), pt_tm(r, rt).
// ci_fs_at(c, r): `from_string` call c on receiver r, by their terms. ci_fs_named(c): its receiver is named like an
// environment, in a file that builds no sandbox.
.decl ci_fs_at(c: symbol, r: symbol)
ci_fs_at(ct, rt) :- ci_fs(c, r), pt_tm(c, ct), pt_tm(r, rt).
.decl ci_fs_named(c: symbol)
ci_fs_named(ct) :- ci_fs(c, r), ci_env_named(r), docof(c, d), !ci_sandbox_doc(d), pt_tm(c, ct).
// ci_xfs(c, how): `from_string` call c is a sink: of a Django template (how "dj") or another ("tpl").
.decl ci_xfs(c: symbol, how: symbol) cross_file
ci_xfs(ct, "dj") :- ci_fs_at(ct, rt), ci_xek(rt, "dj"), !ci_xek(rt, "sb").
ci_xfs(ct, "tpl") :- ci_fs_at(ct, rt), ci_xek(rt, "env"), !ci_xek(rt, "sb"), !ci_xek(rt, "dj").
ci_xfs(ct, "tpl") :- ci_fs_at(ct, rt), ci_fs_named(ct), !ci_xek(rt, "sb"), !ci_xek(rt, "dj").
// ci_env_callee(f): callee f builds a template environment: a library class, or a class of the run deriving from
// jinja2's Environment that no sandbox class is an ancestor of (the phase py_names).
.decl ci_env_callee(f: node)
ci_env_callee(f) :- sym_of(f, q), ci_env_class(q).
ci_env_callee(f) :- sec_run_class(f, q), docof(f, d), doc(d, p, _), py_names__reads_at(p, m),
    py_names__ancestor(m, q, b), ci_env_class0(b), !ci_sandbox_callee(f).
.decl ci_env_class(q: symbol)
ci_env_class("jinja2.Environment"). ci_env_class("jinja2.environment.Environment").
ci_env_class("jinja2.nativetypes.NativeEnvironment"). ci_env_class("django.template.Engine").
ci_env_class("django.template.engine.Engine").
.decl ci_env_class0(q: symbol)
ci_env_class0("jinja2.Environment"). ci_env_class0("jinja2.environment.Environment").
ci_env_class0("jinja2.nativetypes.NativeEnvironment").
// ci_env_named(r): receiver r is named like a template environment: its last name contains env, engine or jinja.
.decl ci_env_named(r: node)
ci_env_named(r) :- leaf_name(r, x), (icontains("env", x) ; icontains("engine", x) ; icontains("jinja", x)).

// ci_sandbox_call(r): r builds a jinja2 sandboxed environment: a library sandbox class, or a class of the run
// deriving from one (the phase py_names).
.decl ci_sandbox_call(r: node)
ci_sandbox_call(r) :- kind(r, "call"), field(r, "function", f), ci_sandbox_callee(f).
.decl ci_sandbox_callee(f: node)
ci_sandbox_callee(f) :- sym_of(f, q), ci_sandbox_class(q).
ci_sandbox_callee(f) :- sym_of(f, q), docof(f, d), doc(d, p, _), py_names__reads_at(p, m), py_names__ancestor(m, q, b),
    ci_sandbox_class(b).
.decl ci_sandbox_class(q: symbol)
ci_sandbox_class("jinja2.sandbox.SandboxedEnvironment"). ci_sandbox_class("jinja2.sandbox.ImmutableSandboxedEnvironment").
// ci_sandbox_doc(d): document d builds a sandboxed environment, so its unresolved environment receivers may be one.
.decl ci_sandbox_doc(d: number)
ci_sandbox_doc(d) :- ci_sandbox_call(c), docof(c, d).

// ---- verified payloads -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ci_hmac_checked(a): deserializer argument a reads a name that its function also passes to an hmac call
// (`hmac.new(key, blob, …)`, `hmac.compare_digest(…)`): the payload is verified against a server key.
.decl ci_hmac_checked(a: node)
ci_hmac_checked(a) :- sec_reads(a, x), nearest(a, h, fscope), kind(c, "call"), sec_call_q(c, q), prefix("hmac.", q),
    nearest(c, h, fscope), call_arg(c, _, _, b), sec_reads(b, x).

